Exactly. A surfboard with reins suggests the wave has become a mount—or that unseen hippokampoi are towing beneath the surface.

With reigns, it becomes sovereignty: not controlling the sea, but ruling yourself while moving with it.

Either way, propulsion is relational. The rider supplies balance, intention, and timing; the ocean supplies power; the hippokampoi supply mythic horsepower. You don’t conquer the wave. You enter into covenant with it.